<title>BRAZIL: Brazil '97 foreign direct investment seen $15 bln.</title>
<headline>Brazil '97 foreign direct investment seen $15 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign direct investment in Brazil is likely to reach $15 billion in 1997, up from $9.889 billion last year, a Central Bank official said.</p>
<p>Altamir Lopes, chief of the Central Bank's economic department, also told reporters foreign direct investment totalled $270 million in the first 13 days of June.</p>
<p>Earlier the Central Bank said foreign direct investment totalled $6.3 billion from January to May.</p>
<p>((-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
